$DIR/main.p:31:10: onPanic3 cannot be the panic handler: it is a method
    The runtime calls the panic handler, the function marked //pu:panic, with a
    description of the panic, and never expects it to return. It is a plain
    function with a body, not a method, not generic and not also an interrupt
    handler, that takes a *rt.Panic and returns nothing.
    A kernel has no operating system to fall back on when it panics, so
    Plutonium makes the program choose what happens at compile time, and checks
    the choice: the runtime calls the handler directly, with nothing to
    register, so it works from the first instruction.
    Declare it:
        //pu:panic
        func onPanic3(p *rt.Panic) { ... }
    (see "Panics in freestanding programs" in the Plutonium spec, section 17.4)
    (run "pluto explain E2582" for a longer explanation)

